  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Here's the prototype actually running and the most important lesson it taught us, which is: don't chase perfection.",
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 6.139
    },
    {
      "text": "Look at this.",
      "start": 6.44,
      "end": 6.98
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if a single apartment comes out right eighty percent of the time, the errors pile up across a dozen apartments, the odds the whole building is right drop to around SEVEN percent.",
      "start": 7.219,
      "end": 16.039
    },
    {
      "text": "That's just how complex systems go little errors compound, and perfect is off the table.",
      "start": 16.5,
      "end": 21.1
    },
    {
      "text": "But the fix is simple, at least in principle: don't make one design, make a whole bunch and filter for the good ones.",
      "start": 21.52,
      "end": 27.119
    },
    {
      "text": "The catch is that filtering means telling good architecture from bad automatically.",
      "start": 27.659,
      "end": 31.699
    },
    {
      "text": "And that's why everything from here on is about EVALUATION because in a system like this, being able to judge the result is the thing that makes it usable at all.",
      "start": 32.02,
      "end": 39.739
    }
  ]
